{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>The sciatic nerve.</b> It is known as our early predecessors of blessed memory transmitted, and there is no doubt about it except among the witless and their ilk who interpret it as the organ. And they interpret הנשה from the root נשים, to demonstrate that this angel who appeared to Jacob was a body. This will be explained to you, if HaShem opens your heart, in the pericope of \"for My name is within him\" (Exodus 23:21)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Resolved קדמונינו ז\"ל as 'our early predecessors of blessed memory'; the term could also refer specifically to rabbinic sages, but the generic rendering preserves Ibn Ezra's range of reference."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:53.945531319Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}